Both files are written. Here's a summary of every change made and why.


.env (created fresh)

Key                    Value / note
---------------------- -------------------------------------------------------
APP_ENV                production
APP_LOG_LEVEL          warning  (less noise than "info" in prod)
SECRET_KEY             CHANGE_ME placeholder — must be set
DB_*/REDIS_*           Credentials with CHANGE_ME placeholders
REDIS_URL / CELERY_*   Constructed from the individual REDIS_* vars so they
                       stay in sync automatically
HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL  15s  (tighter than the staging 30s default)
EMAIL_*, AWS_*, SENTRY External service endpoints — all CHANGE_ME


docker-compose.yaml (what changed vs staging)

Service    What changed
---------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------
web        replicas 1 -> 3 | CPU 0.5->2.0, RAM 512M->2G | volume ./src removed
           (no live-editing in prod) | upload volume -> /srv/widget/uploads bind
           mount | healthcheck retries 3->5 + start_period 30s
worker     replicas 1 -> 3 | same resource bump | --concurrency=4 flag added |
           healthcheck added | depends_on db+redis added
scheduler  replicas stays 1 (Celery Beat must be a singleton) | DatabaseScheduler
           used for persistence | resource limits raised slightly
db         CPU 1.0->4.0, RAM 1G->4G | port bound to 127.0.0.1 only (security) |
           volume -> /srv/widget/pgdata | pg_isready healthcheck added
redis      CPU 0.25->1.0, RAM 256M->1G | maxmemory 1gb + allkeys-lru set |
           port bound to 127.0.0.1 | volume -> /srv/widget/redis-data |
           save 60 1 for persistence | healthcheck added
nginx      replicas 1 -> 2 | port 443 added | TLS/certbot volumes mounted |
           conf changed staging.conf -> production.conf
volumes    All staging-* named volumes removed; bind mounts under /srv/widget/
           used instead for easier backups and OS-level snapshots

Action items before deploying:
1. Replace every CHANGE_ME value in .env with real secrets.
2. Create host directories: sudo mkdir -p /srv/widget/{uploads,pgdata,redis-data,certbot/conf,certbot/www}
3. Add nginx/production.conf (TLS-aware config pointing to the web service).
